  "reason": "Complete construction and prerequisite audit; see research/phase-2-next-20-batch-4.notes.md and coverage.json. Source V, Theorem 2.35 pp.19–20; documented alternative-proof disposition, no raw fetch claim. Each increment of A is integrable and F_{k-1}-measurable by CE. For k<=n these sigma-algebras lie inside F_{n-1}, so A_n is predictable; finite sums are L1. The difference M=X-A is adapted L1. With Delta A_n already known at time n-1, linearity gives E[Delta M_n|F_{n-1}]=E[Delta X_n|F_{n-1}]-Delta A_n=0. Thus M is a martingale. Conversely any decomposition forces E[Delta X_n|F_{n-1}]=Delta A_n, since Delta M_n has conditional mean zero and Delta A_n is known. Induction from A_0=0 forces A and then M. The countable union of equality-exception sets is measurable and null, establishing simultaneous uniqueness without requiring completeness. AC is inherited from the Radon–Nikodym construction of conditional expectation; if a sequence of versions is needed, AC selects measurable versions at the countably many times. Identities remain identities of almost-sure classes, without completing the filtration.",
